[{:db/id 17592186161930 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-24af5ca9-8d38-530b-8002-d4db8feaa5d7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161745 :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X\\sim \\textrm{Exp}\\left(1\\right),$ calculate $P\\left(X < 2\\right).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda$ has the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/f3/f3440005b2b4e7ce1cc2eed5825d11cb309522a6807bcd18ffada189fadd0cda.svg)\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX\\sim \\textrm{Exp} \\left( 1 \\right).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/1f/1f2f28b0f36aeb85a07076e1507c9561b707bf7d00de727998b02075b5458da4.svg)\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P\\left(X < 2\\right)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<2) & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{{e}^{-x}|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2}+{e}^{0} \\\\  & ≈0.8647\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161931 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0be3a602-67d5-5cf7-8f80-aff71640198e" "question-9e3c60ce-47c9-5c4f-b8dd-973c8222fab3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161746 :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X\\sim \\textrm{Exp}\\left(\\dfrac 23\\right),$ calculate $P\\left(X \\geq 3\\right).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda$ has the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/49/49fa146efc8029727469bc5909c2a946c9cb96383976d4096d455b423a428479.svg)\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX\\sim \\textrm{Exp} \\left( \\dfrac 23 \\right).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/72/721ca1810b816431f99bb8294f4ad12ff125342640a925035487c8ecace4eff6.svg)Therefore, we can calculate $P\\left(X \\geq 3\\right)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 3) & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{3}{e}^{-2x/3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{{e}^{-2x/3}|}_{3}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-2} \\\\  & ≈0.1353\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161932 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-548f5527-3c2c-5249-846d-012dddb74912"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161747 :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X\\sim \\textrm{Exp}\\left(2\\right),$ calculate $P\\left(\\dfrac 12 < X < 2\\right).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda$ has the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/e7/e77daa45c1026175eec99e71cb336ad5b8c2a46683170b0f9357a4ad7e9d1bf5.svg)\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX\\sim \\textrm{Exp} \\left( 2 \\right).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/e0/e0b6d1388350fabce97f26601d512e60cfe6ac3ab41230671718ca034c5c3860.svg)Therefore, we can calculate $P\\left(\\dfrac 12 < X < 2\\right)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\frac{1}{2}<X<2) & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{2}2{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{{e}^{-2x}|}_{1/2}^{2} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-4}+{e}^{-1} \\\\  & ≈0.3496\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161933 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-840fc6bd-43f7-5e1f-9678-e0daa00596e7" "question-b6017236-d9af-57fe-9a24-c8e569cb2642"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161748 :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X\\sim \\textrm{Exp}\\left(4\\right),$ calculate $P\\left(X \\leq 7 \\, \\bigg |\\, X > 5\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "Given a random variable $X \\sim \\mathrm{Exp}(\\lambda)$ and two positive real numbers $s, t,$ the memoryless property of the exponential distribution states that\n\n$$\nP(X>s+t \\, \\big |\\, X>s) = P(X > t) = e^{-\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the complementary conditional probability as follows:\n\n$$\nP(X\\leq s+t \\, \\big|\\, X>s) = 1-P(X>s+t \\, \\big |\\, X>s) = 1-e^{-\\lambda t}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda = 4,$ $s=5,$ and $s+t=7.$ From this, we can find $t$ as follows:\n\n$$\nt = (t+s) - s =7 - 5 = 2\n$$\n\nSubstituting these values into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 7\\,|\\,X>5) & =1-{e}^{-\\lambda t} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-(4)\\cdot (2)} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-8} \\\\  & ≈0.999\\,664.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162685 :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(2),$ calculate $P(X<\\frac{1}{6}).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(2).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-2x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X<\\frac{1}{6})$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<\\frac{1}{6}) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/6}2{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2x}{|}_{0}^{1/6} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-1/3}+{e}^{0} \\\\  & ≈0.2835\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161402 :answer-field/correct 17592186161406 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-24af5ca9-8d38-530b-8002-d4db8feaa5d7" :question/id #uuid "24af5ca9-8d38-530b-8002-d4db8feaa5d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-96345" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{3}{4}),$ calculate $P(X<1).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{3}{4}).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{-3x/4}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X<1)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<1) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{-3x/4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-3x/4}{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-3/4}+{e}^{0} \\\\  & ≈0.5276\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c78b8e7b-777c-5193-bc20-a17bf3a58b7b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c78b8e7b-777c-5193-bc20-a17bf3a58b7b" :answer-field/id #uuid "c78b8e7b-777c-5193-bc20-a17bf3a58b7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e0577aef-a54a-5b56-9e1d-4dcfbccf5fde" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2a753c6c-3899-5081-81c1-9c51956a63b5" "answer-e0577aef-a54a-5b56-9e1d-4dcfbccf5fde" "answer-39d93c58-7d48-5de8-9930-8560bb4ab222" "answer-f293deb7-7ba9-56a2-ae3f-b82352272b8d" "answer-b5df255f-d5f8-5d26-a865-2d00936b6ac3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a753c6c-3899-5081-81c1-9c51956a63b5" :answer/id #uuid "2a753c6c-3899-5081-81c1-9c51956a63b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4150" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0577aef-a54a-5b56-9e1d-4dcfbccf5fde" :answer/id #uuid "e0577aef-a54a-5b56-9e1d-4dcfbccf5fde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5276" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39d93c58-7d48-5de8-9930-8560bb4ab222" :answer/id #uuid "39d93c58-7d48-5de8-9930-8560bb4ab222" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5932" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f293deb7-7ba9-56a2-ae3f-b82352272b8d" :answer/id #uuid "f293deb7-7ba9-56a2-ae3f-b82352272b8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.6187" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b5df255f-d5f8-5d26-a865-2d00936b6ac3" :answer/id #uuid "b5df255f-d5f8-5d26-a865-2d00936b6ac3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.6585" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0be3a602-67d5-5cf7-8f80-aff71640198e" :question/id #uuid "0be3a602-67d5-5cf7-8f80-aff71640198e" :question/math-academy-id "q-96406" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(1),$ calculate $P(X\\ge 2).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(1).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X\\ge 2)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 2) & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x}{|}_{2}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-2} \\\\  & ≈0.1353\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-06adbee9-5f6f-500e-9c80-babe38453b76"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-06adbee9-5f6f-500e-9c80-babe38453b76" :answer-field/id #uuid "06adbee9-5f6f-500e-9c80-babe38453b76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cd0cfc25-ccc8-5d6f-a075-ad935990a0fd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3f517b2d-d281-5139-846d-3d24808ad7b5" "answer-cd0cfc25-ccc8-5d6f-a075-ad935990a0fd" "answer-2c1745b6-630b-529f-9136-c40f62c94d25" "answer-7c7853be-90ec-5040-a947-22a3b32a3ad5" "answer-e72eff5e-65c2-554e-894e-cea3af368c6a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f517b2d-d281-5139-846d-3d24808ad7b5" :answer/id #uuid "3f517b2d-d281-5139-846d-3d24808ad7b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0821" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd0cfc25-ccc8-5d6f-a075-ad935990a0fd" :answer/id #uuid "cd0cfc25-ccc8-5d6f-a075-ad935990a0fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1353" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c1745b6-630b-529f-9136-c40f62c94d25" :answer/id #uuid "2c1745b6-630b-529f-9136-c40f62c94d25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2231" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c7853be-90ec-5040-a947-22a3b32a3ad5" :answer/id #uuid "7c7853be-90ec-5040-a947-22a3b32a3ad5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.6065" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e72eff5e-65c2-554e-894e-cea3af368c6a" :answer/id #uuid "e72eff5e-65c2-554e-894e-cea3af368c6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.8647" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9e3c60ce-47c9-5c4f-b8dd-973c8222fab3" :question/id #uuid "9e3c60ce-47c9-5c4f-b8dd-973c8222fab3" :question/math-academy-id "q-96407" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $U∼\\text{Exp}(2),$ calculate $P(U\\ge 3).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $U$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(u)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda u}, & u\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nU∼\\text{Exp}(2).\n$$\n\nSo, $U$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(u)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-2u}, & u\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(U\\ge 3)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(U\\ge 3) & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }f(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-2u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2u}{|}_{3}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-6} \\\\  & ≈0.0025\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0782fde0-7971-5f6d-aba6-4b1f607a9ca1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0782fde0-7971-5f6d-aba6-4b1f607a9ca1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0782fde0-7971-5f6d-aba6-4b1f607a9ca1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9ef5aef2-1def-50a9-8422-76dce776ddf1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9ef5aef2-1def-50a9-8422-76dce776ddf1" "answer-95ffeb01-adda-57d6-881e-fcb39a8b7a3c" "answer-3b8a2e77-056b-5c7d-a4a5-f0b85875f98a" "answer-4e91c1c2-03b1-5f7b-accf-22d6915d4b08" "answer-f083723d-90d7-5c3f-8b0b-f6cf96ee2b97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ef5aef2-1def-50a9-8422-76dce776ddf1" :answer/id #uuid "9ef5aef2-1def-50a9-8422-76dce776ddf1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0025" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95ffeb01-adda-57d6-881e-fcb39a8b7a3c" :answer/id #uuid "95ffeb01-adda-57d6-881e-fcb39a8b7a3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0067" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b8a2e77-056b-5c7d-a4a5-f0b85875f98a" :answer/id #uuid "3b8a2e77-056b-5c7d-a4a5-f0b85875f98a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0498" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e91c1c2-03b1-5f7b-accf-22d6915d4b08" :answer/id #uuid "4e91c1c2-03b1-5f7b-accf-22d6915d4b08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2865" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f083723d-90d7-5c3f-8b0b-f6cf96ee2b97" :answer/id #uuid "f083723d-90d7-5c3f-8b0b-f6cf96ee2b97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3679" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162686 :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{1}{2}),$ calculate $P(1<X<4).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{1}{2}).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x/2}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(1<X<4)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<X<4) & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x/2}{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2}+{e}^{-1/2} \\\\  & ≈0.4712\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161408 :answer-field/correct 17592186161409 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-548f5527-3c2c-5249-846d-012dddb74912" :question/id #uuid "548f5527-3c2c-5249-846d-012dddb74912" :question/math-academy-id "q-96417" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(2),$ calculate $P(1\\le X\\le 3).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(2).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-2x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(1\\le X\\le 3)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1\\le X\\le 3) & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}2{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2x}{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-6}+{e}^{-2} \\\\  & ≈0.1329\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-64885566-dbce-53b8-b813-e5b5f9f5627a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-64885566-dbce-53b8-b813-e5b5f9f5627a" :answer-field/id #uuid "64885566-dbce-53b8-b813-e5b5f9f5627a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6fadb770-777f-5d25-8c8e-520eb1a7bac1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4d1edc2d-b633-52ba-85a7-13aec31489a3" "answer-6fadb770-777f-5d25-8c8e-520eb1a7bac1" "answer-78e06ba4-70f9-51bf-9980-6444eb5316e8" "answer-20637901-6ccf-5b0b-8845-93cfcc926093" "answer-09a50814-795d-5d28-8e92-209754c2af10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d1edc2d-b633-52ba-85a7-13aec31489a3" :answer/id #uuid "4d1edc2d-b633-52ba-85a7-13aec31489a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1286" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6fadb770-777f-5d25-8c8e-520eb1a7bac1" :answer/id #uuid "6fadb770-777f-5d25-8c8e-520eb1a7bac1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1329" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78e06ba4-70f9-51bf-9980-6444eb5316e8" :answer/id #uuid "78e06ba4-70f9-51bf-9980-6444eb5316e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1358" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20637901-6ccf-5b0b-8845-93cfcc926093" :answer/id #uuid "20637901-6ccf-5b0b-8845-93cfcc926093" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3611" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09a50814-795d-5d28-8e92-209754c2af10" :answer/id #uuid "09a50814-795d-5d28-8e92-209754c2af10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3654" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-840fc6bd-43f7-5e1f-9678-e0daa00596e7" :question/id #uuid "840fc6bd-43f7-5e1f-9678-e0daa00596e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-253929" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(2),$ calculate $P(X>6\\,|\\,X>4).$" :question/worked-solution "Given a random variable $X∼Exp(\\lambda ),$ and two positive real numbers $s,t,$ the momeryless property of the exponential distribution states that\n\n$$\nP(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=P(X>t)={e}^{-\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =2,$ $s=4,$ and $s+t=6.$ From this, we can find $t$ as follows:\n\n$$\nt=(t+s)-s=6-4=2\n$$\n\nSubstituting these values into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>6\\,|\\,X>4) & ={e}^{-\\lambda t} \\\\  & ={e}^{-(2)\\cdot (2)} \\\\  & ={e}^{-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-37078ec0-a9a2-5952-8060-4f2067bef6bb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-37078ec0-a9a2-5952-8060-4f2067bef6bb" :answer-field/id #uuid "37078ec0-a9a2-5952-8060-4f2067bef6bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-71609beb-d000-5d09-b83b-5c7ae828643f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a4655f58-d989-5a50-8b84-0a0259d6d8f3" "answer-71609beb-d000-5d09-b83b-5c7ae828643f" "answer-31d5edd8-2b29-5eba-8a70-917a5b0f20f3" "answer-a59b312d-c446-5a83-97bf-18385fce9ef9" "answer-bd231bf4-aff5-5dd1-9238-2dee00cd6f1e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4655f58-d989-5a50-8b84-0a0259d6d8f3" :answer/id #uuid "a4655f58-d989-5a50-8b84-0a0259d6d8f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2{e}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-71609beb-d000-5d09-b83b-5c7ae828643f" :answer/id #uuid "71609beb-d000-5d09-b83b-5c7ae828643f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-31d5edd8-2b29-5eba-8a70-917a5b0f20f3" :answer/id #uuid "31d5edd8-2b29-5eba-8a70-917a5b0f20f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{8}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a59b312d-c446-5a83-97bf-18385fce9ef9" :answer/id #uuid "a59b312d-c446-5a83-97bf-18385fce9ef9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{9}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd231bf4-aff5-5dd1-9238-2dee00cd6f1e" :answer/id #uuid "bd231bf4-aff5-5dd1-9238-2dee00cd6f1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{{e}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b6017236-d9af-57fe-9a24-c8e569cb2642" :question/id #uuid "b6017236-d9af-57fe-9a24-c8e569cb2642" :question/math-academy-id "q-253938" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(2),$ calculate $P(X\\le 9\\,|\\,X>6).$" :question/worked-solution "Given a random variable $X∼Exp(\\lambda ),$ and two positive real numbers $s,t,$ the memoryless property of the exponential distribution states that\n\n$$\nP(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=P(X>t)={e}^{-\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the complementary conditional probability as follows:\n\n$$\nP(X\\le s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=1-P(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=1-{e}^{-\\lambda t}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =2,$ $s=6,$ and $s+t=9.$ From this, we can find $t$ as follows:\n\n$$\nt=(t+s)-s=9-6=3\n$$\n\nSubstituting these values into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 9\\,|\\,X>6) & =1-{e}^{-\\lambda t} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-(2)\\cdot (3)} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e05b810e-c24f-55a7-bef2-0f820b29550d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e05b810e-c24f-55a7-bef2-0f820b29550d" :answer-field/id #uuid "e05b810e-c24f-55a7-bef2-0f820b29550d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e23b4a6b-fba0-5d93-9ac6-0cd62b1a9f21" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5ba4d575-3c96-585c-87ae-967c1404dc69" "answer-00532a77-8369-5069-a645-da39692238cd" "answer-e23b4a6b-fba0-5d93-9ac6-0cd62b1a9f21" "answer-6cf46d04-45a1-535e-a92e-c9cb35404ba7" "answer-950530ce-1ae8-509e-b4cd-ed8ae399b36c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ba4d575-3c96-585c-87ae-967c1404dc69" :answer/id #uuid "5ba4d575-3c96-585c-87ae-967c1404dc69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-2{e}^{-3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-00532a77-8369-5069-a645-da39692238cd" :answer/id #uuid "00532a77-8369-5069-a645-da39692238cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-3{e}^{-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e23b4a6b-fba0-5d93-9ac6-0cd62b1a9f21" :answer/id #uuid "e23b4a6b-fba0-5d93-9ac6-0cd62b1a9f21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-{e}^{-6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6cf46d04-45a1-535e-a92e-c9cb35404ba7" :answer/id #uuid "6cf46d04-45a1-535e-a92e-c9cb35404ba7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{e}^{-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-950530ce-1ae8-509e-b4cd-ed8ae399b36c" :answer/id #uuid "950530ce-1ae8-509e-b4cd-ed8ae399b36c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163182 :tutorial/content "A continuous random variable $X$ follows an **exponential distribution** if it has the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/2a/2ae9fdb32ab1b90d11729ead5966100d53b722ce182eacfb58ff9dc7d037993f.svg)\n\nThe **rate parameter** $\\lambda$ is a positive real number, and $e\\approx 2.71828$ is Euler's number. \n\nIf a random variable $X$ follows an exponential distribution, we write\n\n$$\nX\\sim \\textrm{Exp}(\\lambda).\n$$\n\nThe exponential distribution models the amount of continuous space or time between two events. In a future lesson, we will learn how to model situations using the exponential distribution. But for now, let's get some practice working with the PDF to compute probabilities." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163183 :tutorial/content "Consider a random variable $X \\sim \\mathrm{Exp}(\\lambda),$ and two positive real numbers $s, t.$ \n\nSuppose we're given that  $X>s,$ and we want to determine the probability that $X>s+t.$ In other words, we wish to compute the conditional probability \n\n$$\nP(X>s+t \\,\\big|\\, X>s).\n$$\n\n \n\nBy the definition of conditional probability, we have that\n\n$$\nP(X>s+t \\, \\big|\\, X>s) = \\dfrac{P\\big((X> s+t) \\cap (X > s)\\big)}{P(X>s)}.\n$$\n\nNotice that $X>s+t$ implies that $X>s,$ therefore\n\n$$\nP\\big((X> s+t) \\cap (X > s)\\big) = P(X > s+t).\n$$\n\nSo, the above conditional probability simplifies to\n\n$$\nP(X>s+t \\,\\big|\\, X>s) = \\dfrac{P(X> s+t )}{P(X>s)}.\n$$\n\nNext, let's recall how to calculate $P(X > a)$ for some $a>0{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>a) & =1-P(X<a) \\\\  & =1-{\\int }_{0}^{a}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1+{{e}^{-\\lambda x}|}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =1+{e}^{-\\lambda a}-{e}^{0} \\\\  & ={e}^{-\\lambda a}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can use this fact to calculate $P(X> s+t )$ and $P(X>s)$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s) & =\\frac{P(X>s+t)}{P(X>s)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-\\lambda (s+t)}}{{e}^{-\\lambda s}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-\\lambda s}\\cdot {e}^{-\\lambda t}}{{e}^{-\\lambda s}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{e}^{-\\lambda s}}\\cdot {e}^{-\\lambda t}}{\\cancel{{e}^{-\\lambda s}}} \\\\  & ={e}^{-\\lambda t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, notice that $e^{-\\lambda t} = P(X > t).$ So, we have proved the following property:\n\n$$\nP(X>s+t \\big| X>s) = P(X > t).\n$$\n\nThis property is called **memoryless property.** It can be proved that the exponential distribution is the only continuous distribution with this property (note that the geometric distribution is the only *discrete* distribution with the memoryless property).\n\nIntuitively, the memoryless property states that the probability of an event occurring after a certain amount of time has already elapsed is independent of how much time has passed. This means that the distribution \"forgets\" what has happened before time $s.$ \n\nWe'll discuss how the memoryless property is used for mathematical modeling in future lessons." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163185 :tutorial/content "Given that the random variable $X\\sim \\textrm{Exp}(2),$ let's calculate the following probability:\n\n$$\nP\\left(X > \\dfrac32 \\,\\bigg|\\, X > \\dfrac12\\right)\n$$\n\nGiven a random variable $X \\sim \\mathrm{Exp}(\\lambda)$ and two positive real numbers $s, t,$ the memoryless property of the exponential distribution states that\n\n$$\nP(X>s+t \\, \\big|\\, X>s) = P(X > t) = e^{-\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\lambda = 2, \\qquad s=\\dfrac 12,\\qquad s+t=\\dfrac32.\n$$\n\nFrom this, we can find $t$ as follows:\n\n$$\nt = (t+s) - s = \\dfrac32-\\dfrac12 = 1\n$$\n\nSubstituting these values into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>\\frac{3}{2}\\,|\\,X>\\frac{1}{2}) & ={e}^{-\\lambda t} \\\\  & ={e}^{-(2)\\cdot (1)} \\\\  & ={e}^{-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}} \\\\  & ≈0.135\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162203 :activity/expected-seconds 840.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
